{"_meta": true, "kind": "ablation-single-mechanism", "family": "F1", "mechanism_disabled": "security.content_firewall", "commit": "2ecbdc8", "config_hash": "ablate:security.content_firewall@99bca4da", "note": "Single-mechanism ablation for F1: security.content_firewall disabled, everything else on. 11 trials; crossed=11, unauthorized effects=10. Ablation is compiled in only under MIX_ENV=test. Paper \u00a76.5 / \u00a79.1; spec/ABLATION.md.", "caveat": "Gate-channel ablation: every converted trial carries `effects_observed: []`. For gate families the gate IS the membrane, so a conversion is tainted input traversing it, not a provider-boundary crossing \u2014 no effect-log record exists. These conversions are therefore NOT evidence that the Oracle's effect log fires; only the F4 (16) and F8 (4) ablations produced observed effects. Correcting a claim in paper \u00a76.7."}
